From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:26:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 098/144] GreatDANE: sign-only.sh round 3: DANE_ARCH allowlist,
 no dmg overwrite, realpath guards, ad-hoc mode (NGD R2-M3, LOW)

- R2-M3: DANE_ARCH must be exactly universal|arm64|x86_64, checked before any rm -rf "$STAGE". The version
  string is validated too. An existing dmg is refused and never removed or overwritten (the rm -f and
  hdiutil -ov are gone). New DANE_OUT picks another output dir; it's refused if too broad (/, /Volumes/X,
  /Users/X).
- The source/target guard works on realpaths through the signer's `guard-path`, a single implementation that
  covers /Volumes/Dane*, DaneNotarized, the GreatDANE profile, /Applications, ~/Applications and attached owner
  dmgs on any mount point. It also refuses DANE_APP_SRC inside the stage dir and a symlinked stage dir.
- Ad-hoc throwaway check run: DANE_SIGN_IDENTITY=- skips the keychain and timestamps, keeps hardened runtime
  and per-binary entitlements, runs check without --strict (ad-hoc reported as expected-not-Developer-ID), and
  writes Dane-<ver>-mac-<arch>-ADHOC.dmg. Developer ID runs now use `check --strict`.
- DANE_SIGN_ALLOW_VOLUMES is exported only when the stage is under /Volumes. The stage is passed as
  DANE_SIGN_WORK_DIRS. Any argument is refused (legacy modes retired).
- greatdane/tests/sign_only_selftest.py: 18 cases (stub ditto/xattr/hdiutil/security, mock codesign).
